-one to many ,eg:author and book ,one auther can have multiple books
-many to one implimentation 
-pagination and filtering in graphql
-args take input from the user()
-many to many relationship implimentation
-In GraphQL, a resolver (or “resolve function”) is the function responsible for providing the value for a particular field in your schema()
-In GraphQL, args (short for arguments) is a parameter passed into a resolver function. It represents the set of input values that the client provides in the query (or mutation) for that particular field.